---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<StaticPage path="/dmca/" h1="DMCA and copyright notices" updated={SITE.legalUpdated}>
  <p class="mt-6">
    Opus Calculator respects the rights of copyright owners. If you believe something on the site infringes your copyright, you can send a notice using the
    process below. Notices and counter-notices go to the designated contact: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email.dmca}`}>{SITE.email.dmca}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Sending a takedown notice</h2>
  <p>Please include all of the following, in writing, so that we can act on it:</p>
  <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>Your name, address, telephone number and email address.</li>
    <li>A description of the copyrighted work you say has been infringed, and where it can be seen (a link, if possible).</li>
    <li>The web address (URL) of the page on Opus Calculator that has the material you say infringes, so we can find it.</li>
    <li>A statement that you have a good-faith belief that the use is not authorised by the copyright owner, its agent or the law.</li>
    <li>
      A statement that the information in your notice is accurate and, under penalty of perjury, that you are the copyright owner or authorised to act for the
      owner.
    </li>
    <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>A notice that leaves these out may not be actionable. Knowingly making a false claim can make you liable for damages.</p>

  <h2>What we do with a notice</h2>
  <p>
    When we receive a complete notice we review it promptly. If it appears valid, we remove or disable access to the material, and we may tell the person who
    published it so they can respond. We may keep a record of the notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Sending a counter-notice</h2>
  <p>If material was removed and you believe that was a mistake, you can reply with a counter-notice that includes:</p>
  <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>Your name, address, telephone number and email address.</li>
    <li>A description of the material that was removed and where it appeared before it was removed.</li>
    <li>A statement, under penalty of perjury, that you have a good-faith belief the material was removed because of a mistake or misidentification.</li>
    <li>
      A statement that you consent to the jurisdiction of the courts for your address (or, outside the United States, of any court where the site's owner can be
      found), and that you will accept legal service from the person who sent the original notice.
    </li>
    <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    We pass a valid counter-notice to the person who sent the original notice. Unless they tell us within 10 to 14 business days that they have started court
    action, we may restore the material.
  </p>

  <h2>Repeat infringers</h2>
  <p>In suitable circumstances, we will remove material from, or restrict, a source that repeatedly infringes copyright.</p>

  <h2>Not a legal service</h2>
  <p>This page describes our process. It is not legal advice. If you are unsure of your rights, talk to a lawyer.</p>
</StaticPage>
